# Architecture: Domain Layer

- The domain layer must contain pure business rules and remain framework-independent.
- Module domain code must live under `app/modules/<module>/domain`.
- Use `entities.py`, `enums.py`, `exceptions.py`, `repositories.py`, and `services.py` for standard domain files.
- Domain code may contain entities, enums, value objects, domain exceptions, repository interfaces, and service interfaces.
- Repository interfaces defined in the domain must end with `Repository`.
- Service interfaces defined in the domain must end with `Service`, `Provider`, `Client`, or `Hasher`.
- Domain code must not import FastAPI, SQLAlchemy, Pydantic, Redis, external SDKs, infrastructure implementations, or localization services.
- Domain code must not contain HTTP concepts, HTTP status codes, request/response schemas, ORM models, localized messages, or infrastructure logic.
- Domain exceptions must carry stable error codes instead of raw user-facing text.
- Stable business error codes must use `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`.
